T:Zdravets
T:Geranium: Bulgarian horo song in 9/16
C:traditional (Bulgaria)
O:Bulgaria
R:horo
S:Vasil Stoin, Narodna pesnopoyka (Sofia, 1930), No. 102 "Zdravets", p. 98
N:THE WORDS (Stoin, modern spelling): "Здравче, венче, берат ли те моми?" / "Та мене ли моми да не берат? / Като цъфтя, все гора мирише. / Като дойде на ден на Гергьовден, / те си дойдат хубави девойки, / та ме берат във нови цедила, / та ме носят на бързи потоци, / та ме вият на зелени венци / и ме турят на вакли агънца."
N:IN ENGLISH (ours): "Little geranium, little wreath, do the girls pick you?" / "How could the girls not pick me? When I bloom the whole forest smells sweet. When St George's Day comes, the pretty girls come, they pick me into new cloths, carry me to swift streams, weave me into green wreaths and put me on the dark-eyed lambs."
N:TRANSLITERATED: Zdravche, venche, berat li te momi? / Ta mene li momi da ne berat? / Kato tsaftya, vse gora mirishe. / Kato doyde na den na Gergyovden, / te si doydat hubavi devoyki, / ta me berat vav novi tsedila, / ta me nosyat na barzi pototsi, / ta me viyat na zeleni ventsi / i me turyat na vakli agantsa.
N:THE PLATE: Stoin, "Бързо" (fast), 9/16 with one flat, two lines of three bars with repeat marks at each line's end, the question under both lines, the answer printed as verse below. Each bar is three eighths and a dotted eighth (2+2+2+3), except the last bar, whose last group is an eighth and a sixteenth rest.
N:HOW READ (2026-11-10): p. 98 from the archive.org scan, enlarged three times; staff lines found by row darkness; each head measured by its ink against the staff-only columns beside it and read again on enlargements labelled line by line; every bar checked to make nine sixteenths. The repeat marks are left out here: the words, sung two lines to a pass, give the repeats.
N:UNCERTAIN: the second note of bar 3 in each line (c, measured nearer c than B); the tempo is ours (Stoin gives only "fast").
